{
  "raw": {
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Alumnae-House-Operations-Manager_R00035856": {
      "title": "Alumnae House Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nDepartment Alumnae House Inn Job Family Administrator Vassar College is deeply committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees by promoting an environment of transparency and respect for differences. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds who meet the qualifications of a posting. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu . Job Description Position Summary The Alumnae House Operations Manager is a critical role, reporting directly to the General Manager (GM). This position is responsible for the seamless and efficient daily operation of the Inn's lodging and the Conference Center's event spaces. The ideal candidate is a hands-on, detail-oriented leader with a passion for hospitality, staff management, and ensuring exceptional guest and client experiences. This role requires the ability to work flexible hours, including weekends and holidays, based on the needs of the Inn and Conference Center. This position is a 2- year contract role with the possibly for extension. Alumnae House is a 20-room, 100 year-old, Tudor-style inn and conference center that also serves as the headquarters for Vassar’s Office of Advancement and Alumnae/i Association (AAVC). Responsibilities:  Operational Management Manage and oversee all daily operational activities of the Inn and Conference Center. Liaise with the Vice President of Advancement’s Executive Assistant to ensure the custodial duties related to office and public spaces throughout the building are properly executed. Ensure all facilities are maintained to the highest standards of cleanliness, safety, and operational excellence. Monitor inventory levels for all operational areas (lodging, housekeeping, and conference services) and coordinate supply ordering. Serve as the primary point of contact for the Facilities Operations department and all external vendors (including linens and other suppliers). Manage all service requests and timely execution. Staff Supervision & Leadership Schedule, supervise and manage the performance of the unionized Reservations Specialists (part-time CWA), Custodial and Housekeeping (full-time SEIU) staff. Coordinate and execute training programs for direct reports to ensure consistent service delivery and adherence to operational procedures. Ensure staff schedules meet adequate coverage for all operational hours. Support the General Manager as a front-facing point of contact when the GM is unavailable. Conference & Event Execution Oversee the timely and accurate execution of all set-ups for meetings and catered events, including tables, chairs, staging, and Audio/Visual (A/V) equipment. Act as the on-site point of contact for event clients to ensure all operational needs and last-minute requests are addressed promptly and professionally. Maintain a working knowledge of A/V equipment and troubleshoot minor technical issues during events. Guest Services & Reservations Ensure the Reservations Specialists deliver excellent customer service, manage guest check-ins/outs, and handle guest inquiries or complaints efficiently. Collaborate with the General Manager to ensure rates, black-out dates, and other occupancy requirements are properly managed in the online reservation system. Manage the online reservation software and liaise with vendors to troubleshoot any issues as they arise (including OTAs). Financial & Administrative Provide operational reports to the General Manager, as requested. Monitor operational expenses and ensure adherence to departmental budgets. Coordinate with HR on any matters related to staffing and supervision. Required knowledge, skills and abilities Minimum of 3-5 years of progressive experience in hospitality management, hotel operations, or conference services. Proven ability to lead, motivate, and manage diverse teams, including front-of-house and back-of-house staff. Strong organizational, multitasking, and problem-solving skills. Proficiency with Property Management Systems (PMS) and standard office software (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite). Familiarity with basic event A/V set-up and operation is essential. Ability to work flexible hours, including weekends and holidays, based on the needs of the Inn and Conference Center. Ability to interact effectively with a diverse community. Ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time. Preferred knowledge, skills and abilities Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Two years of supervisory experience.  Compensation  The compensation for this position is $65,000 - $70,000 per year. When extending an offer, Vassar College considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, budget, and other market and organizational considerations. The starting salary range represents the College’s good faith and reasonable estimate at the time of posting. Special Instructions to Applicants: To complete your application, you will be required to attach your resume and cover letter."
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Cafe-Manager_R00035860": {
      "title": "Cafe Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nDepartment Campus Dining - Retreat Job Family Administrator Vassar College is deeply committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees by promoting an environment of transparency and respect for differences. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds who meet the qualifications of a posting. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu . Job Description Position Summary Reporting to the Director of Operations, the Cafe Manager provides day-to-day operational leadership for assigned Dining Services operations. The Cafe Manager maintains a strong and visible presence on the floor, ensuring that dining facilities are appropriately staffed, organized, safe, and operating to established standards for service, food presentation, sanitation, and customer experience. The Cafe Manager supervises Dining Services Supervisors and provides direction, coaching, and accountability to dining employees. The position collaborates with the Director of Operations, Executive Chef, other Cafe Manager, Dining Staffing Manager, and Bon Appétit and Vassar Dining leadership to support a cohesive and effective dining operation. Responsibilities Provide visible and approachable, day-to-day leadership on the dining floor and ensure assigned operations are appropriately staffed, organized, and operating effectively. Supervise and provide direction, coaching, training, and accountability to Dining Services Supervisors and dining employees including unionized staff reviews and coaching sessions in accordance with the collective bargaining agreement. Monitor food presentation, service, sanitation, safety, cleanliness, and overall guest experience, addressing concerns promptly. Participates in monthly safety audits. Work with the Dining Staffing Manager to support staffing, scheduling, employee deployments, call-outs, and coverage needs. Support catering and other Dining Services operations as assigned, including staffing, logistics, event execution, and coordination with campus departments. Collaborate with the Executive Chef, culinary team, Vassar College, and Bon Appétit staff to ensure integrated operations and seamless coordination between culinary production and dining services. Partner with the Campus Dietitian in addressing any special dietary needs and ensure labeling of menu items in service areas is correct. Communicate, build relationships, and respond to concerns to various stakeholders, including management, students, and staff. Support the implementation of Dining Services policies, procedures, training, and service standards. Identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency, service, staffing, and the student dining experience. Participate in Dining Services meetings, Monthly Safety Meetings, planning, and training. Partner with the Director of Operations and Campus Executive Chef to meet financial labor goals. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and work experience. Three years of progressively responsible experience in food service, hospitality, or a high-volume operational environment. Demonstrated supervisory or management experience, including the ability to coach, mentor, develop, and hold employees accountable. Knowledge of financial, budgetary, accounting, and computational practices within food service operations. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills. Ability to work effectively with employees, students, campus partners, and external partners. Ability to work collaboratively with Vassar College and Bon Appétit employees. Comfort using technology to support scheduling, operational, and administrative functions. Availability and flexibility to work evening and weekend hours year-round to support campus dining. Ability to lift heavy objects up to 30 pounds. Team lift anything greater than 30 pounds. Ability to stand and walk for the duration of a shift using repetitive motion with your upper body to complete tasks. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Degree in culinary arts, restaurant management, or a related field. Experience working in higher education. Experience working in a unionized environment. Experience managing high-volume dining operations and/or catering. ServSafe Certification. Compensation The compensation for this position is $65,200 - $79,000 per year. When extending an offer, Vassar College considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, budget, and other market and organizational considerations. The starting salary range represents the College’s good faith and reasonable estimate at the time of posting."
    },
