s and monitor for freshness and quality. Understanding of FIFO principles with daily rotation of stock and properly date/label products stored in coolers, dry storage, or kitchen areas in proper storage containers. Capacity to operate all of the stations and platforms throughout the dining operation within classification. As the runner, gather ingredients and ice from coolers, freezers and stock rooms for efficient food production and service. Throughout the duration of a shift, at the conclusion of a shift, and in preparation for service the next day, ensure kitchen surfaces including floors as well as equipment, pots, pans and utensils dishes, and flatware are maintained, cleaned, sanitized, and organized appropriately to expected standards. Responsible for the proper use of the dish room equipment using water softener and dish washing chemical disbursement to clean, scrape, wash, and stack dishes, utensils, and cooking equipment.  Execute utility functions such as, but not limited to sweeping, mopping, cleaning up spills, trash removal, compostable collection, breaking down boxes, proper collection of recyclables including cardboard, and cleaning and sanitizing carts and trash receptacles and trash collection areas as needed. Clean and sanitize stations, tables, and counters throughout the operation. Restock dishes, flatware, pots, pans, cups, glasses and utensils. Refill napkin baskets, condiments, and salt/pepper shakers as needed. Make coffee and refill milks, sweeteners, juices, soda, C02, and ensure the beverage areas remain clean and sanitary. Restock open air coolers and serving areas with product, fruit, and other items as needed. Assist with putting chairs on tables at the end of the night. Operate and safely use equipment necessary for the job including dish room equipment, assigned kitchen equipment and elevators. Required knowledge, skills and abilities: Ability to lift heavy objects up to 50 pounds and frequently lift and push, pull or carry up to 30 pounds. Team lift anything greater than 50 pounds. Ability to stand and walk for the duration of a shift using repetitive motion with your upper body to complete tasks. Communicate effectively in English including understanding speaking, reading and writing. Remain within work deployment for the duration of a shift except for scheduled breaks and meal periods. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with staff, students/customers, and management. Serve customers in an efficient and friendly manner while resolving any potential issues, remaining flexible to last minute adjustments, and/or by promptly reporting issues to management. Must help ensure success of the dining program by following Health Department regulations and food safety standards as laid out by Vassar and Vassar’s food contract management company. Use necessary protective equipment per guidelines from Vassar and Vassar’s food contract management company. Properly direct and refer questions as it relates to HACCP principles in the field of sanitation and cooking, and allergen and celiac disease. Preferred knowledge, skills and abilities: 1 year of professional food service experience in a high-volume food service environment. Certification in the National Restaurant Association’s ServSafe course for food safety. Willingness to work overtime when available, as assigned according to seniority guidelines. Pay Rate: $21.39 per hour"
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Office-Specialist--L--Health-Services--Part-Time-_R00035762-1": {
      "title": "Office Specialist- L, Health Services (Part Time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nPart time\n\nDepartment Health Services Job Family Staff - Union Vassar College is deeply committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees by promoting an environment of transparency and respect for differences. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds who meet the qualifications of a posting. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu . Job Description Schedule: Every other weekend, 10:45am - 4:15pm Position Summary The Office Specialist-L at Vassar College plays a crucial role within the Health Services Department, focusing on a variety of medical office administrative tasks that support the smooth operations of the health clinic. The Office Specialist will coordinate with students, employees, administrative, and academic offices to ensure that appointments, meetings, requisitions for repairs, and charges for services are conducted in a professional and timely manner.  This is a part-time (11 hours), in-person, CWA union position for the academic year (42 weeks per year). This position is not eligible for benefits. Responsibilities: Provide administrative support for meetings, calls, department calendar, program preparation, onboarding; prepare documents and medical records, reports, and correspondence, and maintain filing systems. Support reception/front desk interactions, answer phones, respond to inquiries, monitor faxing systems, collect and distribute mail, and maintain office supplies including ordering supplies for and maintaining appearance and securing the front door of the common area daily. Support maintenance scheduled and issues associated with department facilities and equipment, communicate updates to department and facilities/vendors. Supports the budget operations of the office/department: reconcile reports; process invoices; process internal service deliveries; process cash sale orders; ensure expenses are charged to appropriate budget accounts and remain within department allocations; monitor daily medical charges; provide notice if out of alignment. Communicate in multiple modes while maintaining patient privacy and confidentiality with department members, vendors, on-campus offices, alumnae/i, volunteers, students, and/or other off-campus partners to complete departmental tasks. Support in the organization of events and office hours including scheduling, room reservations, completing tasks identified by an event plan, use of templates to make name tags, event programs or other event collateral, communicate with vendors and participants, and order food or supplies.   Attend department events to support the successful execution of the event by welcoming attendees, answering event questions, and referring attendees or vendors to the event host for further information.  Support accurate and secure data entry, retention, data uploading, and utilizing pre-built reports for systems and processes. Assist students with requests regarding follow up appointments including appointment booking, provides support with insurance or payment issues, discharges students after appointments to ensure payments and follow-up paperwork is completed. Required knowledge, skills and abilities: Three years of progressively responsible administrative support experience. Strong computer skills including proficiency with Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite and ability to learn additional technical systems.  Experience working in a healthcare setting. Ability to consistently apply policies and procedures. Strong written and verbal communication skills.  Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to interact effectively with a diverse community.  Ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time. Ability to interact socially with others. Preferred knowledge, skills and abilities Five years of progressively responsible administrative support experience. Associates degree or other higher educational experience. Experience working with software systems including finance and accounting systems, payroll, student information systems, or electronic medical record systems. Compensation The compensation for this position is $20.37 per hour."
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Dance_R00035771": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Dance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nDepartment Dance Vassar College is dedicated to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees and welcomes applications from individuals of all backgrounds. Decisions concerning employment are made on the basis of an individual’s qualifications to contribute to meeting Vassar College’s educational objectives and its institutional needs, which includes promoting a respect for difference and creating a learning environment where students from all backgrounds can thrive. Candidates who can contribute to these goals through their teaching, research, advising, and other activities are encouraged to identify their strengths and experiences in this area. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu Job Description Position Introduction: The Dance department invites applications for a full-time, Assistant or Associate Professor of Dance, to begin in the fall 2027 academic year. We are especially interested in advanced Assistant or recently tenured Associate Professors.  We seek an accomplished artist-scholar with expertise in teaching contemporary and modern dance techniques, a distinguished record of professional creative achievement, and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching within a liberal arts environment. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in contemporary and modern dance technique at beginning through advanced levels, choreograph an original work annually for Vassar Repertory Dance Theatre, and teach seminar and/or lecture courses that examine dance through critical, historical, cultural, and theoretical frameworks. We welcome applicants whose creative and scholarly work advances understandings of dance through diverse cultural, historical, aesthetic, and embodied perspectives. Experience with interdisciplinary artistic and scholarly collaboration is highly valued. The teaching load in the first year is the equivalent of four full credit courses, following which the load is the equivalent of five full credit courses per year, or four plus intensive work with students which typically involves directed student research. Responsibilities will include maintaining an active creative and/or scholarly practice, mentoring and advising undergraduate students in their artistic, academic and professional development.  Additionally, contribution to the curriculum development and continued growth of the department while fostering interdisciplinary collaborations within the department and across the College is expected. Qualifications: Candidates must have a Ph.D., MFA or equivalent professional accomplishment in Dance or a closely related field at the time of appointment with demonstrated excellence in teaching contemporary and modern dance technique at multiple levels as an academic and artist.  A sustained record of professional creative work, including choreography and/or performance is also required.  Candidates must also have demonstrated commitment to inclusive, equitable, and student-centered pedagogy and the ability to contribute to the intellectual and artistic life of a liberal arts college through teaching, creative practice, scholarship, and service. Preference will be given to candidates with previous college-level teaching experience; an active professional network and sustained engagement within the contemporary and modern dance communities; experience developing collaborative projects across artistic disciplines; a record of effective student mentorship and support for students’ academic, artistic, and professional growth; and experience integrating technologies such as video, photography, sound, and digital media into creative practice and/or teaching. Application Materials : Cover Letter and CV Teaching Statement Community Impact Statement ( https://offices.vassar.edu/dean-of-the-faculty/positions/community-impact-statement/ ) Contact information for three references who will provide reference letters upon request.  Note: Candidates will be prompted for the contact information following the submission of the application. Course evaluation material along with Syllabi of courses taught for advanced candidates  Links to videos demonstrating original choreography Portfolio of creative work (can include published writings, choreographic documentation, selected press, or links to videos demonstrating teaching) How to Apply: Applications should be addressed to John Meehan and submitted online at: https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External . Please contact John Meehan at jomeehan@vassar.edu with any questions. Review of applicant materials will begin on October 30, 2026 and will continue until the position has been filled. There is no guarantee that applications received after October 30, 2026 will be reviewed. Pay Transparency Disclosure: The annual base starting salary range for this position is $100,000 to $130,000 (USD). This range includes advanced Assistant Professors as well as recently tenured Associate Professors. When extending an offer of employment, Vassar College considers factors such as (but not limited to) candidate’s education/training, work experience, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations. This salary range represents the College’s good faith and reasonable estimate at the time of posting."
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Per-Diem-Health-Specialist--Certified-Medical-Assistant_R00035667": {
      "title": "Per Diem Health Specialist/ Certified Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nPart time\n\nDepartment Health Services Job Family Staff - Union Vassar College is deeply committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees by promoting an environment of transparency and respect for differences. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds who meet the qualifications of a posting. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu . Job Description Schedule: Per Diem hours for Monday - Friday 8:45am - 5:15pm, Saturday & Sunday, 10:45am- 4:15pm during the Academic Year. Position Summary The Health Specialist/Certified Medical Assistant has both clinical and clerical duties. This is an in-person, per diem position and is not eligible for benefits.  Responsibilities: Preparing the patient for medical visits, outpatient procedures and other physical exams by performing vital signs, updating medical history in the electronic health record, and noting any changes in health status. Performing data entry tasks to document patient records within facility databases and maintaining patient files. Assists with the processing of incoming student medical forms. Assisting as a chaperone for sensitive exams or assisting with bedside outpatient medical procedures. Providing phlebotomy services to students and employees. On-site training to be provided. Processing tissue and lab specimens and entering patient insurance information for outpatient labs. Autoclave instruments and send out weekly spore testing. Performing EKGs when ordered by providers. Obtaining prior authorizations when necessary for providers. Prepping and stocking exam rooms as needed. Providing compassionate and inclusive patient support and care during office visits. Assisting patients with making follow-up appointments and referral appointments to off-campus providers and facilities. Assisting with the management of the office telephone systems; including answering calls and emails and returning messages. Assisting in the front office with greeting patients, checking patients in and out for their appointments, appointment scheduling, and making appointment confirmation reminders. Processing and reconciling the student account charges daily and tracking hold bills. Required knowledge, skills and abilities: Completion of an accredited medical assisting program with a certification. Three years of progressively responsible administrative support experience. Strong computer skills including proficiency with Google Suite, Microsoft Office Suite and ability to learn additional technical systems.  Ability to consistently apply policies and procedures. Ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality. Strong written and verbal communication skills.  Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to interact effectively with a diverse community.  Ability to sit or stand for extended periods of time. Ability to interact socially with others. Preferred knowledge, skills and abilities Previous medical office experience/administrative support. Familiarity with electronic record keeping. Compensation The compensation for this position is $20.37 per hour."
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Assistant-Men-s-and-Women-s-Squash-Coach--40-week-_R00035722": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's and Women's Squash Coach (40 week)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nPart time\n\nDepartment Athletics and Physical Education Job Family Administrator Vassar College is deeply committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees by promoting an environment of transparency and respect for differences. We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds who meet the qualifications of a posting. If you need to request an accommodation to fully participate in the search process, please contact careers@vassar.edu . Job Description Position Summary The  Assistant Men’s & Women’s Squash Coach (40 week) is an administrative position within the Department of Athletics and Physical Education.  This is a part-time, non-benefit eligible, 40-week position requiring weekend, holiday, early morning, and late evening hours.  The 40 weeks will be distributed across the calendar year through mutual agreement by the employee and their direct supervisor. Responsibilities Assist the Head Sport Coach with:  Preparation for and execution of all practice and game plans to include: on-court instruction for practices and games, creation of practice plans, development of game strategies and competitive coaching, scouting, game prep, and video exchange Player and team development to include: team film analysis and analytics, sports performance tech management, academic monitoring, and other player and team development activities Recruitment correspondence and on-campus visits Creation of and engagement in all team activities to include: alum engagement, fundraising, and community-service events Equipment management and reconciliation of equipment expenses Team travel arrangements and reconciliation of team travel expenses Required knowledge, skills and abilities Coaching or playing experience at the collegiate, high school, or club level Ability to work with a diverse group of constituents A valid and unrestricted driver’s license Successful result of a background check Preferred knowledge, skills and abilities Bachelor’s degree Two or more years of coaching experience Certification in CPR, AED, and First Aid is preferred and can be obtained through Vassar College as needed Knowledge and compliance with NCAA and league rules and regulations Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills  Proven ability to promote inclusion, belonging, and positive team culture Compensation The compensation for this position is $15,000 per year."
    },
    "https://vassar.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Vassar-External/job/Poughkeepsie-NY/Assistant-Women-s-and-Men-s-Rowing-Coach--40-week-_R00035717-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's and Men's Rowing Coach (40 week)",
